{
  "_note": [
    "composition-test.json — the failure modes fixtures/visual-test.json cannot express.",
    "",
    "visual-test.json has 109 components and ZERO of them carry `children`, so every",
    "composition-dependent property in it is a no-op that all three runtimes agree on",
    "trivially. Measured: `BlendMode_Multiply` is a red box with mix-blend-mode:multiply",
    "and nothing behind it, so it blends against the flat #1A1A2E capture background;",
    "`Glass_Effect` applies backdrop-filter:blur(10px) over a uniform field, which is",
    "arithmetically the identity. A green row there means nothing was tested.",
    "",
    "Every component below puts a child over a NON-UNIFORM parent, so the compositing",
    "maths has something to get wrong. Each one is paired with a control that differs",
    "only in the property under test — if a runtime ignores the property entirely, the",
    "pair renders identically and that is visible, which a single component is not.",
    "",
    "Deliberately NOT included: real text. `_text` does render real glyphs (the 5x7",
    "bitmap fallback only applies to components without it), but cross-platform text is",
    "the known glyph wall that capped ~50 fixtures at SSIM 0.90-0.949 and is what the",
    "bitmap font was introduced to route around. Adding it belongs with the font-pinning",
    "decision, not here."
  ],
  "components": {
    "Blend_Multiply_OverGradient": {
      "properties": {
        "width": "220px", "height": "90px",
        "background-image": "linear-gradient(90deg, #ffffff 0%, #1a1a2e 100%)",
        "position": "relative"
      },
      "children": {
        "layer": {
          "properties": {
            "position": "absolute", "left": "40px", "top": "20px",
            "width": "140px", "height": "50px",
            "background-color": "#e74c3c",
            "mix-blend-mode": "multiply"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blend_Normal_OverGradient_Control": {
      "_note": "Control for the four blend components: identical geometry, blend-mode normal. Any runtime that drops mix-blend-mode renders every blend case as this.",
      "properties": {
        "width": "220px", "height": "90px",
        "background-image": "linear-gradient(90deg, #ffffff 0%, #1a1a2e 100%)",
        "position": "relative"
      },
      "children": {
        "layer": {
          "properties": {
            "position": "absolute", "left": "40px", "top": "20px",
            "width": "140px", "height": "50px",
            "background-color": "#e74c3c",
            "mix-blend-mode": "normal"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blend_Screen_OverGradient": {
      "properties": {
        "width": "220px", "height": "90px",
        "background-image": "linear-gradient(90deg, #ffffff 0%, #1a1a2e 100%)",
        "position": "relative"
      },
      "children": {
        "layer": {
          "properties": {
            "position": "absolute", "left": "40px", "top": "20px",
            "width": "140px", "height": "50px",
            "background-color": "#3498db",
            "mix-blend-mode": "screen"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blend_Difference_OverGradient": {
      "_note": "difference is the most discriminating blend: it is its own inverse and any channel error shows as a hue shift rather than a lightness shift.",
      "properties": {
        "width": "220px", "height": "90px",
        "background-image": "linear-gradient(90deg, #ffffff 0%, #1a1a2e 100%)",
        "position": "relative"
      },
      "children": {
        "layer": {
          "properties": {
            "position": "absolute", "left": "40px", "top": "20px",
            "width": "140px", "height": "50px",
            "background-color": "#2ecc71",
            "mix-blend-mode": "difference"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blend_Overlay_OverGradient": {
      "properties": {
        "width": "220px", "height": "90px",
        "background-image": "linear-gradient(90deg, #ffffff 0%, #1a1a2e 100%)",
        "position": "relative"
      },
      "children": {
        "layer": {
          "properties": {
            "position": "absolute", "left": "40px", "top": "20px",
            "width": "140px", "height": "50px",
            "background-color": "#f1c40f",
            "mix-blend-mode": "overlay"
          }
        }
      }
    },

    "Backdrop_Blur_OverStripes": {
      "_note": "backdrop-filter needs high spatial frequency behind it or the blur is the identity. Hard-stop stripes give it edges to destroy.",
      "properties": {
        "width": "220px", "height": "90px",
        "background-image": "repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, #ffffff 0px, #ffffff 10px, #16a085 10px, #16a085 20px)",
        "position": "relative"
      },
      "children": {
        "glass": {
          "properties": {
            "position": "absolute", "left": "30px", "top": "20px",
            "width": "160px", "height": "50px",
            "background-color": "rgba(255,255,255,0.2)",
            "backdrop-filter": "blur(8px)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Backdrop_None_OverStripes_Control": {
      "_note": "Control: same translucent panel, no backdrop-filter. A runtime that drops backdrop-filter renders the blur case as this.",
      "properties": {
        "width": "220px", "height": "90px",
        "background-image": "repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, #ffffff 0px, #ffffff 10px, #16a085 10px, #16a085 20px)",
        "position": "relative"
      },
      "children": {
        "glass": {
          "properties": {
            "position": "absolute", "left": "30px", "top": "20px",
            "width": "160px", "height": "50px",
            "background-color": "rgba(255,255,255,0.2)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Backdrop_Saturate_OverStripes": {
      "properties": {
        "width": "220px", "height": "90px",
        "background-image": "repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, #ffffff 0px, #ffffff 10px, #16a085 10px, #16a085 20px)",
        "position": "relative"
      },
      "children": {
        "glass": {
          "properties": {
            "position": "absolute", "left": "30px", "top": "20px",
            "width": "160px", "height": "50px",
            "background-color": "rgba(255,255,255,0.05)",
            "backdrop-filter": "saturate(4)"
          }
        }
      }
    },

    "Overflow_Hidden_ClipsChild": {
      "_note": "Child is deliberately larger than the parent on both axes. If clipping is ignored the child paints outside the parent box, which also changes the capture's measured size.",
      "properties": {
        "width": "160px", "height": "70px",
        "background-color": "#34495e",
        "overflow": "hidden",
        "position": "relative"
      },
      "children": {
        "big": {
          "properties": {
            "position": "absolute", "left": "40px", "top": "20px",
            "width": "260px", "height": "160px",
            "background-color": "#e67e22"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Overflow_Visible_Control": {
      "_note": "Control: identical geometry, overflow visible. The pair must NOT render identically — if it does, one runtime is ignoring overflow.",
      "properties": {
        "width": "160px", "height": "70px",
        "background-color": "#34495e",
        "overflow": "visible",
        "position": "relative"
      },
      "children": {
        "big": {
          "properties": {
            "position": "absolute", "left": "40px", "top": "20px",
            "width": "260px", "height": "160px",
            "background-color": "#e67e22"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Overflow_Hidden_WithRadius": {
      "_note": "Clipping must follow the border radius, not the border box — the classic corner-bleed bug.",
      "properties": {
        "width": "160px", "height": "70px",
        "background-color": "#34495e",
        "border-radius": "24px",
        "overflow": "hidden",
        "position": "relative"
      },
      "children": {
        "big": {
          "properties": {
            "position": "absolute", "left": "0px", "top": "0px",
            "width": "260px", "height": "160px",
            "background-color": "#e67e22"
          }
        }
      }
    },

    "ZOrder_Ascending": {
      "_note": "Three overlapping siblings with explicit z-index. Paint order is only observable where they overlap, so each pair overlaps by half its width.",
      "properties": {
        "width": "220px", "height": "80px",
        "background-color": "#1a1a2e",
        "position": "relative"
      },
      "children": {
        "a": { "properties": { "position": "absolute", "left": "20px", "top": "15px", "width": "80px", "height": "50px", "background-color": "#e74c3c", "z-index": "1" } },
        "b": { "properties": { "position": "absolute", "left": "60px", "top": "15px", "width": "80px", "height": "50px", "background-color": "#3498db", "z-index": "2" } },
        "c": { "properties": { "position": "absolute", "left": "100px", "top": "15px", "width": "80px", "height": "50px", "background-color": "#2ecc71", "z-index": "3" } }
      }
    },
    "ZOrder_Descending": {
      "_note": "Same three boxes, reversed z-index. Must render as the mirror of ZOrder_Ascending; a runtime that paints in source order renders both identically.",
      "properties": {
        "width": "220px", "height": "80px",
        "background-color": "#1a1a2e",
        "position": "relative"
      },
      "children": {
        "a": { "properties": { "position": "absolute", "left": "20px", "top": "15px", "width": "80px", "height": "50px", "background-color": "#e74c3c", "z-index": "3" } },
        "b": { "properties": { "position": "absolute", "left": "60px", "top": "15px", "width": "80px", "height": "50px", "background-color": "#3498db", "z-index": "2" } },
        "c": { "properties": { "position": "absolute", "left": "100px", "top": "15px", "width": "80px", "height": "50px", "background-color": "#2ecc71", "z-index": "1" } }
      }
    },
    "ZOrder_SourceOrder_NoIndex": {
      "_note": "No z-index at all: painting must follow source order, which should equal ZOrder_Ascending. Pins that the ascending case is not an accident of source order.",
      "properties": {
        "width": "220px", "height": "80px",
        "background-color": "#1a1a2e",
        "position": "relative"
      },
      "children": {
        "a": { "properties": { "position": "absolute", "left": "20px", "top": "15px", "width": "80px", "height": "50px", "background-color": "#e74c3c" } },
        "b": { "properties": { "position": "absolute", "left": "60px", "top": "15px", "width": "80px", "height": "50px", "background-color": "#3498db" } },
        "c": { "properties": { "position": "absolute", "left": "100px", "top": "15px", "width": "80px", "height": "50px", "background-color": "#2ecc71" } }
      }
    },

    "Nested_BoxModel_PaddingBorder": {
      "_note": "The child's containing block is the parent's PADDING box, not its border box. An off-by-one here is a 4px offset that no flat fixture can produce.",
      "properties": {
        "width": "200px", "height": "80px",
        "background-color": "#2c3e50",
        "padding": "16px",
        "border": "8px solid #e74c3c",
        "box-sizing": "border-box"
      },
      "children": {
        "inner": {
          "properties": { "width": "100%", "height": "100%", "background-color": "#f1c40f" }
        }
      }
    },
    "Nested_ThreeDeep": {
      "_note": "Three levels of nesting with padding at each. Accumulated offsets diverge faster than a single level, so a per-level rounding difference is measurable here and invisible in visual-test.json.",
      "properties": {
        "width": "200px", "height": "90px",
        "background-color": "#8e44ad",
        "padding": "10px",
        "box-sizing": "border-box"
      },
      "children": {
        "mid": {
          "properties": { "width": "100%", "height": "100%", "background-color": "#16a085", "padding": "10px", "box-sizing": "border-box" },
          "children": {
            "leaf": {
              "properties": { "width": "100%", "height": "100%", "background-color": "#f39c12" }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Nested_OpacityGroup": {
      "_note": "opacity on a parent creates a stacking context and composites the SUBTREE as a group. Two overlapping children at parent-opacity 0.5 must show the group blend, not each child individually faded — a classic divergence.",
      "properties": {
        "width": "200px", "height": "80px",
        "background-color": "#ffffff",
        "opacity": "0.5",
        "position": "relative"
      },
      "children": {
        "a": { "properties": { "position": "absolute", "left": "20px", "top": "15px", "width": "100px", "height": "50px", "background-color": "#e74c3c" } },
        "b": { "properties": { "position": "absolute", "left": "70px", "top": "15px", "width": "100px", "height": "50px", "background-color": "#2980b9" } }
      }
    }
  }
}
